+@@ -39,6 +39,14 @@ The original image transfer, staging padding, copy-back ranges and independent
+ writer merges remain in place. Input preserves the previous transfer-padding bytes;
+ smaller elements and unsupported grids retain the generic conversion.
+ 
++On iOS with Turnip and unified memory, a foreground pool miss sizes its new
++backing block from the request, rounded to a power of two with a 4 MiB minimum.
++Existing pooled space is still used first, and large or explicitly isolated
++allocations retain their dedicated size. The background room keeper continues
++to grow its reserves up to 64 MiB. This limits the pages synchronously prepared
++by a foreground miss without changing texture contents or transfer ordering;
++it can increase the number of small backing blocks.
++
+ ## Depending on it
+ 
+ Not on crates.io yet. Depend on both crates from the same git revision (or checkout):
